  "method": "Each El Niño winter (DJF ONI of +1.0 or more) is left out in turn and the fit is redone on the other years. A harvest is measured against the average of up to 8 earlier harvests, so no later year informs it. Because yields trend upward, that average runs low. The yardstick is the same fit without its El Niño term (the average of the other years), which carries that trend. 'Sign right' means the fit and the harvest both landed on the same side of the yardstick; beating it means the El Niño term moved the forecast closer to what happened. The 90% band includes year-to-year noise.",
